To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries in row 3 other than $a_{32}=-3$ equal to $0.$

To do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:

$$
\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 & 4 & 6 \\ 3 & -4 & -6 & -6 \\ -3 & -3 & 6 & 12 \\ 5 & 1 & -4 & -2\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}-C_{2}}\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 4 & 6 \\ 7 & -4 & -6 & -6 \\ 0 & -3 & 6 & 12 \\ 4 & 1 & -4 & -2\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}+2C_{2}}\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 0 & 6 \\ 7 & -4 & -14 & -6 \\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 12 \\ 4 & 1 & -2 & -2\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{4}:=C_{4}+4C_{2}}\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 0 & -2 \\ 7 & -4 & -14 & -22 \\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\ 4 & 1 & -2 & 2\end{bmatrix}=B
$$

Therefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are

$C_{3}:=C_{3}+2C_{2}$ and $C_{4}:=C_{4}+4C_{2}$.

